{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Summary\n\nCausal numerical reports and persisted GCM requests now reach fresh Scientist consumers with complete source-bound canonical-payload checks. The final F transfer binds all 35 original findings/17 bundles to exact source cards, code SHA/tree, actual consumers, full oracle/removal outputs and separate technical outcomes:17 closed,16 limited,2 held. G integration and formal ledger acceptance remain pending.\n\nThe final index covers15 immutable science/runtime components across 12 topic PRs. Fetch this branch for the documentation and separate handoff receipt; use the exact pinned component refs and G source-only integration order rather than cherry-picking cumulative branches. Scientific source is unchanged by the final documentation commits. The consumer slice owns 7 source/test/release paths and explicitly carries 43 dependency paths in its assembled 50-path candidate.\n\n## Change Categories\n\n- [x] runtime behavior\n- [x] docs\n\n## Compatibility Classification\n\n- [x] internal\n\n## Labels and Ownership\n\n- [x] At least one kind label, exactly one compat label and one release label applied.\n- [x] Owned areas: Scientist causal consumer bindings, associated tests/release fragment, F E02 Git evidence/transfer documents.\n- [ ] Affected owners have completed review.\n\n## Rollout Ownership\n\n- Migration/review owner: G integrates reviewed source-only F topics; C/A/E retain their contract and shared-writer ownership.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe frozen source receipts retain actual Python 3.14 application consumers, pinned Python 3.12 DoWhy 0.14 worker, native NetworkX 3.6.1 mixed parallel-edge readback, clean-room sharp RDD RBC vs rdrobust 2.1.0 oracle, and independent analytic/DGP/graph controls. Rebuilt wheel and sdist both pass genuine worker and latest B220 consumer tests; complete outputs are committed in their pinned topics.\n\nThe committed final index verification passes35IDs/17 bundles/15components/12topics/36cardbindings(35distinct)/137full-byte transports. Independent review and coherent missing-component/wrong-owner/stale-hash/open/pending/swapped-card controls pass. Full removed-property outputs retain their actual expected FAILs.\n\nCurrent deciding reference custody passes. All-reference custody remains UNRUN solely one unavailable historical provenance blob 175c1ed4db37589e8adaf14af6700ad639edb2c8 (four non-deciding references, local absence and GitHub 404 preserved); no F 35 closure uses it. Whole architecture prerequisites UNRUN; measured docs/static/EMP FAIL/ERROR and P41 `not_established` remain explicit. Optional backend SKIP is never PASS; source/law/history/authority-dependent production reruns remain local to G. No main publication or permanent cleanup.\n\n## Docs\n\n- [x] Final entry point: policy-engine/docs/research/e02-cloud-test-plan/implementation-handoffs/F/final-transfer-20261006/REPORT.md and index.json.\n- [x] G local rerun recipe, safe source-only integration order, doctor admissions, full lossless custody audit and exact cleanup candidates committed.\n\n## Rollback / Mitigation\n\nG may decline any source component independently. Existing source mechanisms retain typed refusal/limited states for unresolved data, graph, law, estimator and authority inputs. Do not infer production closure from a bounded synthetic PASS.\n\n## Release Notes Fragment\n\n- [x] Existing causal consumer release fragment covers the runtime change; the final transfer adds documentation only.\n\nPublished closeout topic head after push/readback:421f1dd977b237307394c68820caab4156716eb2 (tree0508db0976255da2d970168d1300ec6dbafcb1b2). Documentation implementation:73f1e698f4271983ed8e83fba0314ca1f36b5a48/tree86845947252bee585eb7293d49f3d0b333a5c6f0; separate courier receipt at E02/implementation-handoffs/F/final-transfer-20261006.json. Fresh main remains198076863e143dea9f89f02734b13d50dae3eed5/tree2b754a92c27959e2e747738d47ed0b419f3b6dd8, published anchor confirmed ancestor. All12 exact remote topic heads read back; final24 validation and9 critical document byte bindings checked.\n","headRefName":"codex/e02-F-closeout-20261006","headRefOid":"f17b9a52784d9484ef65563dc6695240629bdfc6","isDraft":true,"mergedAt":null,"state":"OPEN","title":"fix(scientist): bind causal consumers and publish F 35-finding Git transfer","url":"https://github.com/DenisKopylov/polisyos/pull/65"}
